   "notes": "shore shelf water tile (32 x 28 octagon, 7 x 7 chamfers; seams X -9..9 / Y -7..7; ground 0, bed 0.2, water 0.25 -> 1.0, foam 1.03 -> 1.07, sand crest 1.6, turf 10.4): a flat cyan water plate with a pale sand shelf, one faceted sea stack (three columns, a spire, two shoulder blocks) under a lime grass cap with ferns, lime leaves, daisies and buds; six chunky flat-crowned side rocks in soft lobed foam, a foam ribbon round the shelf. One closed land shell; the cap, plants and sand pebbles their own shells; closed water and foam shells (two water pieces). Still water (no flow). 13 water_foam sockets"
